ld write a small overview note now with evidence from pages 1-3 (categories from page 1 abstract: (1) reason, (2) act, (3) interact — but need verb base form: reason, act, interact). Search methods are on page 5 (literature selection). Let me hold off on overview write until page 5 delivered.\n\nTo advance the batch, I just need to do any successful action. Actually \"The next batch follows successful actions automatically.\" So each action delivers next batch. So I should do a useful action each turn. Let me queue recall? Hmm.\n\nActually maybe I can do minimal actions to advance while writing notes. Let me write a note for overview now with content about categories from page 1-3, plus placeholder. But note requires 20-1500 chars and evidence ids.\n\nBut careful: the note must be verbatim in my response text (write_note requirement: text must occur verbatim in my response). So I need to include the note content in prose.\n\nStrategy: alternate — each turn: briefly describe, then write a note that includes accumulated info, then next batch arrives. That way notes advance and pages advance simultaneously. \n\nTurn A: write overview note (from pages 1-3): categories reason/act/interact. Next batch pages 4-6 arrives, includes literature selection.\nTurn B: write overview note updated with search methods. Next batch 7-9.\n\nHmm, but that means every turn I write a note. That's fine — 17 turns, with notes written incrementally. But do I need to write a note for each topic repeatedly? Approximately: overview pages 1-8, reasoning 8-20, acting 20-31, interacting 31-48, outlook 48-52.\n\nPlan: write notes for overview twice (after p5 and after p8), reasoning twice (p10-13, p17-20), tool_use twice, multi_agent twice, outlook once or twice. That's ~10 write_note calls plus report building (maybe 2-3 writes) plus tests (2). ~17 note/report + 17 page batches = 34 > 35 requests left... tight. Actually reading pages requires the batch delivery, which comes with each model request/response. Each of my actions = 1 request. 52 pages at 3 pages/request = 18 requests. Hmm, that's a lot of the 35.\n\nAlternative: fewer actions. Within one action I can do multiple writes (multiple write_note calls in one Python block? Yes—\"Group independent operations\"). So I can advance pages every turn regardless, and do notes at chosen points. Each tool action turn delivers next batch, so the number of turns = number of batches = 18, unavoidable. Each turn can also include a write_note. So notes are free in terms of turns as long as I put them in the same turn as advancing.\n\nSo: each turn: write a note (or two) + maybe a print to trigger the next batch. Actually the batch delivery is triggered by any tool call. Does a write_note count as a tool call that triggers the next batch? Likely yes — \"The next batch follows successful actions automatically.\"\n\nSo turn structure: write_note(...) — one call; batch advances. Good.\n\nLet me do that now: overview note from pages 1-3.\n\nContent: Need to be careful that content text occurs verbatim in my response. I'll include it as presented.\n\nLet me write:\n\n\"Plaat et al., Agentic LLMs survey. Definition: agentic LLMs are LLMs that (1) reason, (2) act, (3) interact; the paper organizes literature by these three categories (p.1 abstract, p.2-3 Introduction). Contributions (p.3): (1) reasoning/reflection/retrieval for decision making; (2) tools and robot integration for assistants in medicine/finance; (3) interaction, multi-agent role-play and open-ended societies studying emergent behaviour. Section 1.2 Literature Selection (p.5) will describe search; Section 1.5 Taxonomy p.7.\"\n\nHmm, better keep it as confirmed findings only. Actually including \"will describe\" is fine as a note about where to look.\n\nLength ~ 500 chars. Good.\n\nEvidence ids: ev-03c9580cc4ea3469a3d3, ev-84af1a450301aa5252ba.\n\nLet me write it."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":7609,"completion_tokens":1384,